 <following up my own post>

  Zap wand of teleport at the square should move all the items to a
"safe" dry land square somewhere else on the level.  They are unlikely
to all end up on the same square.

  I just noticed from your post that you have wands of cancellation in
the moat as well.  That's the big worry removed.  

  Next time, just drop the BoH first so you'll still have everything
else.  Of course, if you keep your BoH blessed in the future, there
won't be a next time.  (I spent 200k turns once with random malignant
auras and a polearm I did *not* want to end up cursed and welded to my
hands.  It never once went from blessed to cursed from a single curse
attack.)



  Also, barbarians can get to "skilled" in attack spells.  If you have
the spell of cone of cold (or can get it) this could be helpful. 

  Barbarians are the worst spell casters in the game.  I doubt if you've
bothered to optimize your stats/armor for spell casting.  It also seems
unlikely that you've learned spells or #enhanced attack spells.  You
probably don't have much Pw either.  (20 is the minimum needed to cast 
cone of cold.)

  Still, it's something to do while waiting for something more useful to
come along.  You probably left behind some spell-casting-enhancing robes
on the Moloch's Sanctum level, as well as some spellbooks.  Going back
down to get them would also let you scavenge all the levels for possibly
useful items.  

  If you get the spell of cone of cold, careful use of it while wearing
a robe and no spell-hostile armor may be enough.  If not, careful
practice with an easier attack spell under the same conditions should
let you enhance attack spell skill enough to cast cone of cold.
(Between the damage it does and the ability to freeze lava/water cone of
cold may be the single most useful spell in the game.)  

  Of course, as a barbarian you may never have enough max pwr to cast
cone of cold in the first place.  "[E]ach attempt to cast a spell drains
energy equal to 5 times the spell's level (randomly up to three times
this amount if you have the Amulet) for a successful casting, or half as
much for a failure."  Cone of Cold is a level 4 spell, so a minimum of
20 power is required.

 


  Your wand of cancellation strategy for disenchanters is perfect.
Still, here are some alternate strategies in case you need them before
recovering your wands of cancellation:

  - Use non-enchanted weapons.  Some players carry a non-enchanted
artifact weapon for just this purpose.  Remember, you still get your
strength damage bonus (which can be as high as +6 with 18/** or 25 Str.)

  - Throw rocks/gems/glass/darts/daggers at them from a safe distance.
They all do about +2 damage, but rocks/daggers weigh ten times as much.
They also all add in your strength damage bonus.  Daggers have an
intrinsic +2 to-hit bonus and won't disappear.  All the other missiles
may disappear.

  - Use a negatively enchanted (but not cursed) weapon.  "Your silver
saber seems more effective."  (Not great, just amusing.)

  - Shuriken should average about 3 damage to disenchanters and have an
intrinsic +2 to hit.  So they're good ranged weapons even for those
classes, like barbarians, that are restricted in the skill.  Shuriken
also get your strength damage bonus.  They may disappear.

  - As a barbarian, you can get to basic skill with a bow/arrows.  The
upside is that there are probably a lot of these lying around.  "Fire
and forget", to misuse the term.  The downside is the possibility of
getting the bow cursed and welded to your hand.  Very bad.  (You also do
NOT get the strength damage bonus.)  Bamboo arrows (aka "ya") have an
intrinsic +1 to-hit bonus.  Arrows do around 4 damage, when they hit.
Arrows also may disappear.



